Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: apps/list.c
Line: 1109
Function: list_objects
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: OBJ_nid2sn(i) and OBJ_nid2ln(i) can legally return NULL per the OpenSSL API. At line 1109 they are passed to BIO_printf with %s without a NULL check, which will dereference a NULL pointer and crash for objects that lack a short and/or long name.

Source context:
